# Kaiki
/database/*.sqlite
/database/*.sqlite-journal
/database/*.sqlite-shm
/database/*.sqlite-wal
/public/widget
# The widget's build output and its workspace modules. The bundle is published
# by the release pipeline (ADR-0011), never committed — a checked-in artefact is
# one somebody edits by hand.
/packages/*/dist
/packages/*/node_modules
# The ENV-10 snapshot is committed as database/schema/*.snapshot.sql. A dump at
# either of Laravel's own schema paths would be loaded INSTEAD of running the
# migrations, so a stray one must never reach a commit. The .dump extension is
# the one MigrateCommand::schemaPath() checks FIRST, and the connection name is
# part of the filename, so this covers sqlite-schema.sql on a local machine too.
/database/schema/*-schema.sql
/database/schema/*-schema.dump
# Written by `composer test:coverage`; the figure belongs in CI, not in a commit.
/coverage.xml
/.claude/agent-memory
/.claude/settings.local.json


# The end-to-end run: a database it recreates, a key it mints, and its output.
/database/e2e.sqlite
/packages/widget/e2e/.state.json
/packages/widget/e2e/.results
/playwright-report

# The WordPress plugin brings its own dev dependencies; the release zip carries
# a production vendor/ built by the workflow, not this one. The lock file **is**
# committed, so the linter everybody runs is the same linter.
/packages/wordpress-plugin/kaiki-booking/vendor

# The manual's two build products. The chapters, the stylesheet, the capture and
# the screenshots are all committed, so `node docs/manual/build.mjs` reproduces
# both — and a seven-megabyte PDF re-added on every rebuild is a repository
# nobody wants to clone.
/docs/manual/manual.html
/docs/manual/kaiki-manual.pdf

# The WordPress guide's intermediate HTML, for the same reason. Its PDF **is**
# committed, unlike the manual's: it carries no screenshots, so it is under a
# megabyte, and a reader who clones this repository to answer "how does the
# plugin work" should not have to run a build first.
/docs/wordpress/guide.html

# The two presentations and their screenshots, moved into the repository on
# 14 September so the generators stop living in a temporary folder that gets
# swept. The **scripts** are committed — they are the deck; the 46 MB of
# full-resolution PNGs and the two .pptx they produce are not, for the same
# reason the manual's PDF is not. `node docs/deck/shots.mjs docs/deck` and
# `python docs/deck/deck.py` rebuild both from a running Kaiki.
/docs/deck/deck-shots
/docs/deck/*.pptx
/docs/deck-team/shots
/docs/deck-team/preview
/docs/deck-team/*.pptx

# The questions document's intermediate page. Its PDF is written straight to
# the desktop and never into the repository.
/docs/erotiseis/erotiseis.html
/docs/erotiseis/check.pdf

# Mailpit, downloaded rather than committed — 28 MB of binary that
# `docs/testing/` tells you how to fetch (testing only, never production).
/tools/*.exe

# Any copy of the environment file, however it is named. A backup called
# `.env.backup-lan` reached a public repository because the ignore rule was
# the exact name rather than the shape.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local build output
docs/staging/staging.html
packages/wordpress-plugin/kaiki-booking/.phpunit.cache/
